What happens when a critically ill patient is denied a treatment they desperately want to try—and their family must turn to the courts for help?Show more During the COVID-19 pandemic, as hospitalized patients deteriorated under rigid treatment protocols, families across America fought to gain access to ivermectin and other treatments their hospitals refused to administer. For many, attorney Ralph Lorigo became their last hope.\nBetween 2020 and 2022, Lorigo emerged as one of the nation's leading attorneys challenging hospital treatment policies, representing hundreds of families seeking access to alternative COVID-19 treatments. With patients' lives hanging in the balance, he fought urgent legal battles over medical autonomy, informed consent, and the right of patients and families to participate in decisions about their own care.\nA featured speaker at VSRF's COVID Litigation Conference, Lorigo recently testified before a Senate hearing convened by Senator Ron Johnson, recounting what he witnessed as families struggled against hospital policies and legal obstacles while their loved ones fought for survival.\nThis Tuesday, Lorigo joins Steve Kirsch to take us inside those courtrooms, share the stories of the patients and families he represented, and reveal what these battles exposed about the balance of power between hospitals, physicians, and patients.\nWhen a hospital's treatment protocol conflicts with a patient's wishes, who should have the final say? What did these legal battles teach us about the rights of patients and the limits of hospital authority? And what must change to ensure that patients and families never face these battles again?\nTuesday, October 20, at 7 PM ET / 4 PM PT.\nProgramming note: New Zealand whistleblower Barry Young's anticipated court ruling has been delayed by approximately four weeks. Barry is now scheduled to join VSRF Live next month to discuss his case and the court's decision. Show less", "thumbnail": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fww1/a7/s8/1/m/6/c/7/m6c7A.qR4e.3-small-VSRF-Live-250-When-Hosptial..jpg", "display_id": "v7equ8m", "fulltitle": "VSRF Live #250 - When Hosptials Denied The Right To Try", "duration_string": "1:08:54", "upload_date": "20261015", "release_date": "20261020", "release_year": 2026, "is_live": false, "was_live": true, "epoch": 1794326771, "acodec": "aac", "vcodec": "none", "url": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fww1/a7/s8/2/m/6/c/7/m6c7A.Gaa.rec.aac", "format_id": "audio-192p", "tbr": 191, "filesize": 99237443, "width": 0, "height": 192, "protocol": "https", "ext": "aac", "audio_ext": "aac", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 191, "resolution": "audio only", "aspect_ratio": 0.0, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate"}, "format": "audio-192p - audio only", "_type": "video", "_version": {"version": "2026.11.04.232659", "release_git_head": "412e7f0a4b0588fe884a02b344ac66a06538475b", "repository": "yt-dlp/yt-dlp-nightly-builds"}}